1
00:00:00,504 --> 00:00:01,969
Your cat is talking to you all

2
00:00:01,819 --> 00:00:02,529
day long.

3
00:00:02,783 --> 00:00:05,029
Not with words, but with its tail,

4
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:07,777
its ears, its eyes and its whole

5
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:08,323
body.

6
00:00:09,258 --> 00:00:10,840
Most people miss almost all of it.

7
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,859
So in this video, we're going to

8
00:00:12,709 --> 00:00:14,213
learn to read your cat like a

9
00:00:14,076 --> 00:00:16,218
book, one signal at a time.

10
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:19,014
By the end, you'll know when your

11
00:00:18,864 --> 00:00:21,345
cat loves you, when it's scared, and

12
00:00:21,195 --> 00:00:23,155
exactly when to stop petting before you

13
00:00:23,018 --> 00:00:23,675
get bitten.

14
00:00:24,604 --> 00:00:25,353
Chapter one:

15
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:26,317
the tail.

16
00:00:26,596 --> 00:00:28,179
The tail is like your cat's mood

17
00:00:28,042 --> 00:00:30,900
antenna, and it's the easiest signal to

18
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:32,137
read from across the room.

19
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:34,653
A tail held straight up is a

20
00:00:34,517 --> 00:00:35,539
friendly hello.

21
00:00:35,806 --> 00:00:38,091
Cats greet each other this way, and

22
00:00:37,941 --> 00:00:39,575
when your cat walks toward you like

23
00:00:39,425 --> 00:00:41,359
this, it's happy to see you.

24
00:00:42,271 --> 00:00:43,880
If the tip curls over like a

25
00:00:43,743 --> 00:00:45,520
question mark, even better.

26
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,525
That usually means your cat is in

27
00:00:47,375 --> 00:00:50,182
a friendly, curious, playful mood.

28
00:00:51,137 --> 00:00:53,449
And if that upright tail starts to

29
00:00:53,312 --> 00:00:56,430
quiver, your cat is really excited.

30
00:00:56,710 --> 00:00:58,110
It's often what you see when you

31
00:00:57,973 --> 00:01:00,246
come home or open the treat bag.

32
00:01:01,204 --> 00:01:03,047
Now, the warning signs.

33
00:01:03,327 --> 00:01:05,846
A puffed-up tail, like a bottle brush,

34
00:01:06,126 --> 00:01:08,854
means your cat is startled or scared,

35
00:01:09,147 --> 00:01:10,312
and it's trying to look bigger.

36
00:01:11,271 --> 00:01:13,778
A tail held low, or tucked between

37
00:01:13,628 --> 00:01:16,434
the legs, means your cat feels nervous

38
00:01:16,401 --> 00:01:17,398
or unsure.

39
00:01:17,664 --> 00:01:19,260
Give it some space and let it

40
00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:19,911
come to you.

41
00:01:20,884 --> 00:01:22,584
Here's the one people get wrong the

42
00:01:22,434 --> 00:01:23,131
most.

43
00:01:23,397 --> 00:01:25,188
A tail swishing hard from side to

44
00:01:25,038 --> 00:01:27,844
side is not a happy wag, like

45
00:01:27,694 --> 00:01:28,521
in dogs.

46
00:01:28,801 --> 00:01:31,594
In cats, it usually means irritation.

47
00:01:32,504 --> 00:01:35,245
A slow swish, or just the tip

48
00:01:35,108 --> 00:01:38,045
twitching, means your cat is focused, maybe

49
00:01:37,908 --> 00:01:40,376
watching prey, or getting a little annoyed.

50
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:42,732
Pay attention to what comes next.

51
00:01:43,658 --> 00:01:45,227
And when your cat wraps its tail

52
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:47,897
around your leg or your arm, that's

53
00:01:47,747 --> 00:01:49,056
the cat version of a hug.

54
00:01:49,322 --> 00:01:50,722
It's a sign of affection.

55
00:01:51,658 --> 00:01:52,954
Quick recap of the tail:

56
00:01:53,234 --> 00:01:56,378
up means hello, puffed means scared, low

57
00:01:56,228 --> 00:01:59,230
means nervous, and swishing means stop.

58
00:01:59,497 --> 00:02:02,277
If you remember only one chapter, make

59
00:02:02,127 --> 00:02:02,837
it this one.

60
00:02:03,771 --> 00:02:04,585
Chapter two:

61
00:02:04,735 --> 00:02:05,705
the ears.

62
00:02:05,985 --> 00:02:08,257
Cats have more than thirty muscles in

63
00:02:08,237 --> 00:02:10,523
each ear, so they can point them

64
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:11,903
almost anywhere.

65
00:02:12,837 --> 00:02:15,253
Ears facing forward mean your cat is

66
00:02:15,116 --> 00:02:17,766
relaxed, alert or interested.

67
00:02:18,045 --> 00:02:20,005
It's the default position of a calm,

68
00:02:20,077 --> 00:02:21,164
confident cat.

69
00:02:22,091 --> 00:02:24,520
Ears that keep turning like little radars

70
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:27,853
mean your cat is listening carefully, trying

71
00:02:27,703 --> 00:02:29,142
to figure out what's going on around

72
00:02:29,005 --> 00:02:29,324
it.

73
00:02:30,271 --> 00:02:32,778
When the ears turn sideways and flatten

74
00:02:32,628 --> 00:02:35,851
a bit, like airplane wings, your cat

75
00:02:36,026 --> 00:02:38,090
is irritated or anxious.

76
00:02:38,357 --> 00:02:39,666
This is a good moment to back

77
00:02:39,529 --> 00:02:40,083
off.

78
00:02:41,037 --> 00:02:43,127
And ears pressed flat against the head

79
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:45,575
mean real fear, or a cat ready

80
00:02:45,425 --> 00:02:46,734
to defend itself.

81
00:02:47,014 --> 00:02:48,661
Don't reach for a cat with ears

82
00:02:48,511 --> 00:02:49,351
like this.

83
00:02:50,304 --> 00:02:51,274
Chapter three:

84
00:02:51,567 --> 00:02:52,485
the eyes.

85
00:02:52,752 --> 00:02:55,376
Pupils change size with the light, but

86
00:02:55,239 --> 00:02:57,316
they also change with emotion.

87
00:02:58,237 --> 00:03:01,968
Big, round pupils can mean excitement, playfulness

88
00:03:01,831 --> 00:03:02,736
or fear.

89
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:04,155
You need to look at the rest

90
00:03:04,005 --> 00:03:05,484
of the body to know which one

91
00:03:05,334 --> 00:03:06,004
it is.

92
00:03:06,911 --> 00:03:09,574
Narrow, slit pupils in normal light can

93
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:12,803
mean a tense or irritated cat, especially

94
00:03:12,653 --> 00:03:14,327
if the ears and tail agree.

95
00:03:15,271 --> 00:03:17,947
A long, hard stare is a challenge

96
00:03:17,836 --> 00:03:18,833
in the cat world.

97
00:03:19,112 --> 00:03:21,476
That's why cats often walk straight to

98
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:22,973
the one person in the room who

99
00:03:22,823 --> 00:03:23,637
ignores them.

100
00:03:24,558 --> 00:03:26,414
And then there's the slow blink.

101
00:03:26,694 --> 00:03:28,263
When your cat looks at you and

102
00:03:28,113 --> 00:03:31,271
slowly closes and opens its eyes, it's

103
00:03:31,121 --> 00:03:33,224
a sign that it feels relaxed and

104
00:03:33,074 --> 00:03:34,083
safe with you.

105
00:03:35,024 --> 00:03:37,531
In one study, cats were more likely

106
00:03:37,381 --> 00:03:39,901
to approach a stranger who slow blinked

107
00:03:39,751 --> 00:03:40,213
at them.

108
00:03:40,493 --> 00:03:41,737
So you can blink back.

109
00:03:42,003 --> 00:03:43,130
It actually works.

110
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:45,333
One more eye signal:

111
00:03:45,691 --> 00:03:47,312
if your cat dozes off with its

112
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,994
eyes half open near you, or rests

113
00:03:49,844 --> 00:03:51,453
with its eyes closed while you're in

114
00:03:51,303 --> 00:03:53,484
the room, it feels safe enough to

115
00:03:53,347 --> 00:03:54,317
let its guard down.

116
00:03:55,237 --> 00:03:56,155
Chapter four:

117
00:03:56,435 --> 00:03:57,392
the whiskers.

118
00:03:57,646 --> 00:04:00,244
Relaxed whiskers stick out to the sides.

119
00:04:00,524 --> 00:04:03,004
Whiskers pushed forward mean your cat is

120
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:05,439
curious, or focused on something it wants

121
00:04:05,289 --> 00:04:06,103
to catch.

122
00:04:07,037 --> 00:04:09,257
Whiskers pulled back flat against the face

123
00:04:09,251 --> 00:04:12,343
mean your cat is scared or defensive.

124
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:14,791
Combined with flat ears, it's a clear

125
00:04:14,641 --> 00:04:15,560
stop sign.

126
00:04:16,491 --> 00:04:17,514
Chapter five:

127
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:18,217
the body.

128
00:04:18,496 --> 00:04:20,027
A cat sitting like a loaf of

129
00:04:19,877 --> 00:04:22,774
bread, with its paws tucked under, is

130
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,050
comfortable and calm.

131
00:04:24,971 --> 00:04:26,853
A cat lying on its back and

132
00:04:26,716 --> 00:04:29,600
showing its belly is showing huge trust,

133
00:04:29,698 --> 00:04:31,814
because the belly is its most vulnerable

134
00:04:31,677 --> 00:04:32,361
spot.

135
00:04:33,317 --> 00:04:34,170
But careful.

136
00:04:34,424 --> 00:04:36,384
A belly up is not always an

137
00:04:36,247 --> 00:04:37,439
invitation to rub.

138
00:04:37,705 --> 00:04:40,186
Many cats love showing the belly and

139
00:04:40,049 --> 00:04:41,592
hate having it touched.

140
00:04:41,859 --> 00:04:43,454
It's the famous belly trap.

141
00:04:44,378 --> 00:04:45,947
An arched back with all the fur

142
00:04:45,810 --> 00:04:48,981
standing up, the classic Halloween cat, means

143
00:04:48,831 --> 00:04:51,117
your cat is frightened and trying to

144
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:52,627
look as big as possible.

145
00:04:53,511 --> 00:04:55,875
An arched back without puffed fur is

146
00:04:55,738 --> 00:04:56,760
totally different.

147
00:04:57,027 --> 00:04:59,234
That's just a stretch, or a cat

148
00:04:59,214 --> 00:05:00,771
rubbing against you to say hello.

149
00:05:01,691 --> 00:05:03,664
A cat crouched low to the ground

150
00:05:03,527 --> 00:05:05,891
with a tense body is either scared,

151
00:05:06,027 --> 00:05:06,828
or hunting.

152
00:05:07,095 --> 00:05:09,081
Look at the eyes and the tail

153
00:05:09,178 --> 00:05:10,357
to tell the difference.

154
00:05:11,258 --> 00:05:13,335
And that little butt wiggle right before

155
00:05:13,198 --> 00:05:14,025
a pounce?

156
00:05:14,292 --> 00:05:17,007
That's pure hunting instinct, getting the back

157
00:05:16,857 --> 00:05:18,361
legs ready to launch.

158
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:21,518
Finally, when your cat sleeps right next

159
00:05:21,368 --> 00:05:24,577
to you, or on you, it's choosing

160
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:26,374
you as a safe place to be

161
00:05:26,355 --> 00:05:28,054
at its most defenseless.

162
00:05:29,004 --> 00:05:30,612
Also watch where your cat likes to

163
00:05:30,476 --> 00:05:31,029
sit.

164
00:05:31,296 --> 00:05:34,389
Cats love high places, like the top

165
00:05:34,252 --> 00:05:36,303
of the fridge, because from up there

166
00:05:36,153 --> 00:05:38,269
they can watch everything and feel in

167
00:05:38,119 --> 00:05:38,855
control.

168
00:05:39,791 --> 00:05:40,892
Chapter six:

169
00:05:40,976 --> 00:05:41,881
the sounds.

170
00:05:42,148 --> 00:05:44,277
As we saw on this channel, adult

171
00:05:44,127 --> 00:05:47,506
cats mostly meow for us humans, and

172
00:05:47,552 --> 00:05:49,147
each cat builds its own set of

173
00:05:48,997 --> 00:05:49,889
meows.

174
00:05:50,804 --> 00:05:53,623
A short, cheerful meow is usually a

175
00:05:53,486 --> 00:05:54,092
greeting.

176
00:05:54,359 --> 00:05:57,465
A long, drawn-out meow is usually a

177
00:05:57,315 --> 00:06:00,173
demand, often for food or for a

178
00:06:00,036 --> 00:06:00,980
door to be opened.

179
00:06:01,904 --> 00:06:04,059
The trill is that cute rolling sound,

180
00:06:04,118 --> 00:06:06,143
like a mix between a meow and

181
00:06:05,993 --> 00:06:06,716
a purr.

182
00:06:06,969 --> 00:06:08,369
Mother cats use it to call their

183
00:06:08,219 --> 00:06:10,140
kittens, and your cat uses it to

184
00:06:10,003 --> 00:06:12,197
say hi, or follow me.

185
00:06:13,137 --> 00:06:15,123
Purring usually means contentment.

186
00:06:15,403 --> 00:06:17,610
But cats also purr when they're stressed,

187
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:20,253
sick or in pain, probably to calm

188
00:06:20,103 --> 00:06:21,035
themselves down.

189
00:06:21,958 --> 00:06:24,543
So a purring cat that's hiding, not

190
00:06:24,497 --> 00:06:27,160
eating, or acting strange might actually need

191
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:28,475
a vet, not a cuddle.

192
00:06:29,391 --> 00:06:31,924
Chattering is that clicking sound at birds

193
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:32,822
through the window.

194
00:06:33,089 --> 00:06:35,505
It shows excitement, and maybe a little

195
00:06:35,355 --> 00:06:36,325
frustration.

196
00:06:37,237 --> 00:06:38,806
A hiss is a clear warning:

197
00:06:39,099 --> 00:06:39,926
back off.

198
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:43,351
Most hissing cats aren't aggressive, they're scared

199
00:06:43,201 --> 00:06:44,848
and asking for space.

200
00:06:45,771 --> 00:06:47,874
A growl is a stronger warning.

201
00:06:48,141 --> 00:06:50,010
If your cat growls, stop what you're

202
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,169
doing and give it room.

203
00:06:52,091 --> 00:06:53,699
And a loud yowl can mean a

204
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:55,848
cat looking for a mate, a cat

205
00:06:55,698 --> 00:06:58,882
in distress, or in older cats, confusion.

206
00:06:59,135 --> 00:07:00,718
If it's new, it's worth a vet

207
00:07:00,568 --> 00:07:01,147
visit.

208
00:07:02,104 --> 00:07:03,869
And silence can be a signal too.

209
00:07:04,148 --> 00:07:06,186
A cat that suddenly stops making its

210
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:09,233
usual sounds, or starts hiding, might be

211
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:10,900
stressed or unwell.

212
00:07:11,837 --> 00:07:12,690
Chapter seven:

213
00:07:13,061 --> 00:07:14,565
how cats say I love you.

214
00:07:14,858 --> 00:07:17,065
Cats rarely make it obvious, but they

215
00:07:16,915 --> 00:07:18,055
show it all the time.

216
00:07:19,004 --> 00:07:21,198
Head bumps and cheek rubs leave their

217
00:07:21,048 --> 00:07:21,928
scent on you.

218
00:07:22,207 --> 00:07:23,672
You're being marked as family.

219
00:07:24,591 --> 00:07:26,785
Kneading on your lap is a leftover

220
00:07:26,648 --> 00:07:27,606
from kittenhood.

221
00:07:27,872 --> 00:07:29,910
It means your cat feels safe and

222
00:07:29,773 --> 00:07:32,137
happy, like it did with its mother.

223
00:07:33,024 --> 00:07:35,531
Licking you, or grooming your hair, is

224
00:07:35,381 --> 00:07:36,534
called allogrooming.

225
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,382
Cats do it with the cats they're

226
00:07:38,233 --> 00:07:39,112
bonded to.

227
00:07:39,378 --> 00:07:40,284
You're part of the group.

228
00:07:41,237 --> 00:07:44,213
And yes, turning around and showing you

229
00:07:44,076 --> 00:07:45,437
its butt is a compliment.

230
00:07:45,716 --> 00:07:47,846
Cats greet each other by sniffing there,

231
00:07:48,086 --> 00:07:50,450
so your cat is basically saying hello.

232
00:07:51,443 --> 00:07:54,093
Following you from room to room, even

233
00:07:53,943 --> 00:07:56,177
to the bathroom, means your cat wants

234
00:07:56,027 --> 00:07:57,088
to be where you are.

235
00:07:57,329 --> 00:07:58,585
You're its favorite company.

236
00:07:59,517 --> 00:08:02,441
Bringing you prey, sleeping on your clothes,

237
00:08:02,486 --> 00:08:04,238
and greeting you at the door are

238
00:08:04,088 --> 00:08:06,034
all signs of a strong bond.

239
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:09,856
And the slow blink, again, is maybe

240
00:08:09,719 --> 00:08:11,171
the purest one of all.

241
00:08:11,437 --> 00:08:12,447
It's your cat saying:

242
00:08:12,805 --> 00:08:13,632
I trust you.

243
00:08:14,558 --> 00:08:16,909
Even choosing to sit near you, without

244
00:08:16,759 --> 00:08:18,719
touching, is a big deal.

245
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:21,127
For an independent animal, just being in

246
00:08:20,977 --> 00:08:23,028
the same room as you is a

247
00:08:22,878 --> 00:08:23,784
choice.

248
00:08:24,737 --> 00:08:25,577
Chapter eight:

249
00:08:26,078 --> 00:08:27,322
reading the whole cat.

250
00:08:27,602 --> 00:08:29,614
One signal alone can trick you.

251
00:08:29,893 --> 00:08:31,710
The secret is to read the tail,

252
00:08:32,016 --> 00:08:34,640
ears, eyes and body together.

253
00:08:35,623 --> 00:08:38,026
For example, a purring cat with a

254
00:08:37,876 --> 00:08:40,916
lashing tail and ears turning back is

255
00:08:40,779 --> 00:08:41,724
not happy.

256
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:43,794
It's telling you it has had enough.

257
00:08:44,737 --> 00:08:47,309
Some cats get overstimulated when you pet

258
00:08:47,159 --> 00:08:48,220
them for too long.

259
00:08:48,487 --> 00:08:50,343
It can go from purring to biting

260
00:08:50,206 --> 00:08:51,150
in seconds.

261
00:08:52,071 --> 00:08:53,549
Watch for the warning signs:

262
00:08:53,829 --> 00:08:56,323
the tail starts twitching, the skin on

263
00:08:56,186 --> 00:08:59,448
the back ripples, the ears turn sideways,

264
00:08:59,688 --> 00:09:01,375
and the cat stops purring.

265
00:09:02,304 --> 00:09:04,642
When you see those signs, stop petting

266
00:09:04,674 --> 00:09:05,709
and let your cat go.

267
00:09:05,989 --> 00:09:08,340
If you respect the warning, you'll almost

268
00:09:08,190 --> 00:09:09,160
never get bitten.

269
00:09:10,071 --> 00:09:10,937
Chapter nine:

270
00:09:11,243 --> 00:09:12,239
how to speak cat.

271
00:09:12,571 --> 00:09:14,427
First, let the cat come to you.

272
00:09:14,694 --> 00:09:16,497
Offer a finger or a knuckle at

273
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,437
nose height, and let it sniff.

274
00:09:19,384 --> 00:09:21,318
Pet the places cats like most:

275
00:09:21,585 --> 00:09:23,336
the cheeks, under the chin, and the

276
00:09:23,199 --> 00:09:24,326
base of the ears.

277
00:09:24,593 --> 00:09:27,529
Most cats prefer short, gentle strokes there.

278
00:09:28,458 --> 00:09:31,863
Avoid staring, avoid sudden moves, and don't

279
00:09:31,726 --> 00:09:33,660
grab a cat that's trying to leave.

280
00:09:33,927 --> 00:09:35,796
Cats love having the choice.

281
00:09:36,737 --> 00:09:38,241
And use the slow blink.

